.TH "OSTRYA\-LOG" "1" "" "ostrya" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ostrya\-log \- Show the log that starts at a commit or ref
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
ostrya log [OPTIONS] [REV]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Show the log that starts at a commit or ref.
.PP
The command walks the parent chain, newest first. For each commit, it prints \fB\%commit <checksum>\fR and the commit report of \fB\%show\fR\&. If the object of a parent commit is not in the repository, the command prints \fB\%<< History beyond this commit not fetched >>\fR and exits \%0.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIREV\fR
The revision to start at. Required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Show the raw variant data.
.IP
For each commit, the command prints the commit value in the GVariant text form, in place of the commit report.
.PP
The global options are listed in \fBostrya\fR(1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBostrya\fR(1)
